/T (Napkin design)
/E (Napkin design)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Intended for in-city operations that allow for multiple flights during the day. Entering into the enhanced category according to EASA. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Especially inspired for the European market, where there are many major cities that can be easily connected with these aircraft. It is able to adapt to an urban environment with many buildings and few airfields with runways suitable for conventional  take-off and landing.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The eVTOL concept has gained popularity in the last few years, and several companies have already developed their own prototypes, and have even carried out the first test flights. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (But to get to that point they have taken years and a lot of investment behind these ambitious projects.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Generated with AI)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (These vehicles are not only intended to improve urban mobility but also to provide zero carbon solutions as most of them are designed with electric motors.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
