/P 416 0 R
/ActualText (Market opportunity)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Europe's landscape reveals a dense network of potential eVTOL markets, with the highest concentrations appearing in the Western and Central regions. Countries like the United Kingdom, France, Germany, Italy, and Spain demonstrate significant coverage, with urban areas well within the 100 km operational range. This indicates that many European cities could benefit from eVTOL connectivity, enhancing intra-country and cross-border mobility.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the United States, there is a noticeable concentration of potential markets along the East Coast, spanning from the Boston-Washington D.C. corridor to Florida, indicating a high demand for eVTOL services in densely populated areas. The West Coast shows potential markets focused around urban centers like Los Angeles, San Francisco, and Seattle. Inland cities such as Denver and Phoenix also emerge as key areas where eVTOLs could significantly impact transportation dynamics.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Middle East presents an emerging market with urban centers such as Dubai, Riyadh, and Doha poised to adopt eVTOL technologies. The distribution suggests that the range capabilities align well with the geographic spacing of cities in this region, potentially transforming travel and logistics in an area that is rapidly urbanizing and investing in technological advancements.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 417 0 R
/ActualText (Technical data )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The design represents a cutting-edge concept, featuring a combination of six fixed-position engines for takeoff, landing, and low-speed maneuvering. These six engines, equipped with two-blade propellers, are aligned along the longitudinal axis to minimize drag during flight stages where lift is provided by the wings.)
/E (The design represents a cutting-edge concept, featuring a combination of six fixed-position engines for takeoff, landing, and low-speed maneuvering. These six engines, equipped with two-blade propellers, are aligned along the longitudinal axis to minimize drag during flight stages where lift is provided by the wings.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Additionally, the aircraft is equipped with two tilting electric engines utilizing three-blade propellers. This configuration optimizes the thrust-to-weight ratio during vertical takeoff and landing, ensuring enhanced safety and redundancy with a total of eight engines. During horizontal flight, these tilting engines transition to provide thrust while the wings generate lift.)
/E (Additionally, the aircraft is equipped with two tilting electric engines utilizing three-blade propellers. This configuration optimizes the thrust-to-weight ratio during vertical takeoff and landing, ensuring enhanced safety and redundancy with a total of eight engines. During horizontal flight, these tilting engines transition to provide thrust while the wings generate lift.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The pilot and copilot positions are designed to offer the best possible visibility. The tilt-rotor mechanism is strategically placed to optimize lift distribution and maintain a clear area for passenger circulation, fully complying with aviation regulations.)
/E (The pilot and copilot positions are designed to offer the best possible visibility. The tilt-rotor mechanism is strategically placed to optimize lift distribution and maintain a clear area for passenger circulation, fully complying with aviation regulations.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
